<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I'm sorry that my last post was hasty.   It was an incomplete page I was adding to the Cloud section and I did not have time to finish it yesterday.  Nonetheless, I knew that several of you are anxious to start reading about Cloud.   So, it is now an official page called <strong><a href="https://michaelkentburns.com/index.php/cloud/cloud-computing-providers/" data-type="page" data-id="997">Cloud Compute Providers</a>.</strong>  Today I completed the first revision of that page.   I also began another page about <strong><a href="https://michaelkentburns.com/index.php/deploying-to-the-cloud/" data-type="page" data-id="1005">Deploying to the Cloud</a></strong>.   </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On a related topic of testing that you have been heavily engaged in:  I just today came to a verbal agreement with a team that is extending a large and complex LMS (Learning Management System).    <strong>They would like to hire us to start testing </strong>the newest version which is heavily cloud based.    I will begin working with the more senior team members to scope out how we can capitalize on this opportunity. </p>
